[2026-03-14T19:58:22.960Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GN6NE2AdecHaZrnuZhUcNf","type":"tool_result","content":"157:- **Expected**: The sidebar displays a \"Team Section\" with each team name as a collapsible section header. Under each team: \"Issues\" (list icon), \"Active Cycle\" (refresh-cw icon), \"Projects\" (folder icon), \"Views\" (layout icon).\n162:- **Expected**: The team section collapses, hiding Issues, Active Cycle, Projects, and Views sub-links. Clicking again expands it back.\n179:#### Test: Sidebar team Projects link navigates to team projects\n181:- **Action**: User clicks \"Projects\" under the \"Engineering\" team section\n182:- **Expected**: User is navigated to the projects page filtered by this team, or to `/projects` with the team filter applied.\n191:- **Expected**: The sidebar displays a \"Workspace\" section with links: \"All Projects\" (folder icon), \"All Teams\" (users icon), \"Members\" (user-plus icon), \"Labels\" (tag icon), \"Settings\" (settings icon).\n193:#### Test: Sidebar All Projects link navigates correctly\n195:- **Action**: User clicks \"All Projects\" in the workspace section\n196:- **Expected**: User is navigated to `/projects`.\n275:- **Expected**: Team navigation items are still accessible in icon-only mode (icons for Issues, Active Cycle, Projects, Views are visible and clickable).\n279:- **Expected**: Workspace section items (All Projects, All Teams, Members, Labels, Settings) are visible as icons and remain clickable.\n373:- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing My Issues. Issue ENG-42 exists with title \"Fix login bug\", status \"In Progress\", priority \"High\", labels [\"Bug\"], assignee avatar, due date \"2026-03-20\", project \"Auth Rewrite\".\n374:- **Expected**: The issue row displays: High priority icon (orange arrow-up), identifier \"ENG-42\", title \"Fix login bug\", In Progress status icon (yellow half circle), \"Bug\" label as a small colored badge, assignee avatar, due date \"Mar 20\", and project name \"Auth Rewrite\".\n417:#### Test: Issue row shows project name when assigned\n418:- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, issue ENG-42 is assigned to project \"Auth Rewrite\"\n419:- **Expected**: The project name \"Auth Rewrite\" is displayed in the issue row.\n422:- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, issue ENG-43 has no labels, no due date, no project\n423:- **Expected**: The issue row does not show empty placeholders for labels, due date, or project. Only the present fields (priority, identifier, title, status, assignee) are shown.\n616:- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing team issues. Issue ENG-42 exists with title \"Fix login bug\", status \"In Progress\", priority \"High\", labels [\"Bug\"], assignee \"Jane Doe\" (with avatar), due date \"2026-03-20\", project \"Auth Rewrite\".\n617:- **Expected**: The issue row displays: a checkbox for bulk selection (unchecked), High priority icon (orange arrow-up), identifier \"ENG-42\" with team prefix, title \"Fix login bug\", In Progress status icon (yellow half circle), \"Bug\" label as a small colored badge, assignee avatar, due date \"Mar 20\", and project name \"Auth Rewrite\".\n667:- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, issue ENG-43 has no labels, no due date, no project, no assignee\n668:- **Expected**: The issue row does not show empty placeholders for labels, due date, project, or assignee. Only the present fields (checkbox, priority, identifier, title, status) are shown.\n759:- **Expected**: A dropdown opens showing options: Status, Priority, Assignee, Project, Label, None. Each option is clickable.\n771:#### Test: Group by Project groups issues under project headers\n772:- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, team has issues in project \"Auth Rewrite\" (2), \"Dashboard v2\" (1), and no project (1)\n773:- **Action**: User selects \"Project\" from the Group by dropdown\n774:- **Expected**: Issues are grouped under project name headers. A \"No Project\" group shows unassigned issues. Each header shows the project name and issue count.\n839:- **Expected**: A toolbar at the top of the issue list displays filter controls: \"Status\", \"Priority\", \"Assignee\", \"Label\", \"Project\", and \"Cycle\" filters. Each shows as a button/chip that can be clicked to open a dropdown.\n881:#### Test: Project filter dropdown shows all team projects\n882:- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, team has projects \"Auth Rewrite\" and \"Dashboard v2\"\n883:- **Action**: User clicks the \"Project\" filter button\n884:- **Expected**: A multi-select dropdown opens showing \"Auth Rewrite\", \"Dashboard v2\", and a \"No Project\" option. Each has a checkbox.\n886:#### Test: Project filter filters issues by selected projects\n887:- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, team has issues: ENG-1 (project \"Auth Rewrite\"), ENG-2 (project \"Dashboard v2\"), ENG-3 (no project)\n888:- **Action**: User opens Project filter and selects \"Auth Rewrite\"\n1115:- **Initial state**: User is on the issue detail page for an issue with status \"In Progress\", priority \"High\", assignee \"Alice\", labels [\"Bug\", \"Frontend\"], project \"Auth Rewrite\", cycle \"Sprint 3\", due date \"2026-04-01\"\n1116:- **Expected**: The right sidebar displays all property fields: Status showing \"In Progress\" with half-circle yellow icon, Priority showing \"High\" with orange arrow-up icon, Assignee showing \"Alice\" with avatar, Labels showing \"Bug\" and \"Frontend\" as colored badges, Project showing \"Auth Rewrite\", Cycle showing \"Sprint 3\", Due Date showing \"Apr 1, 2026\", Created timestamp (read-only), and Updated timestamp (read-only).\n1170:#### Test: Change project via searchable selector\n1171:- **Initial state**: Issue has no project assigned. Available projects include \"Auth Rewrite\", \"Performance Optimization\", \"Mobile App\".\n1172:- **Action**: User clicks the Project field in the sidebar\n1173:- **Expected**: A searchable dropdown appears listing available projects.\n1175:#### Test: Search and select project\n1176:- **Initial state**: The project dropdown is open\n1178:- **Expected**: The dropdown closes. Project updates to show \"Auth Rewrite\". The change is persisted. An activity entry is created.\n1180:#### Test: Remove project assignment\n1181:- **Initial state**: Issue is assigned to project \"Auth Rewrite\"\n1182:- **Action**: User clicks the Project field, then clicks a \"Remove\" or clear option\n1183:- **Expected**: The project is unassigned. The field shows as empty (e.g., \"No project\"). The change is persisted. An activity entry is created.\n1232:- **Expected**: Modal displays: Team selector dropdown, Title text input, Description text area, Status dropdown, Priority dropdown, Assignee searchable selector, Labels multi-select, Project searchable selector, Cycle dropdown, Due date picker, and Parent issue searchable selector. All fields are visible and properly labeled.\n1316:#### Test: Project selector is searchable\n1317:- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open. Projects \"API Redesign\", \"Mobile App\", \"Dashboard\" exist.\n1318:- **Action**: User clicks the Project selector and types \"API\"\n1321:#### Test: Project selector allows selecting a project\n1322:- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open, Project field is empty\n1323:- **Action**: User clicks the Project selector and selects \"Mobile App\"\n1324:- **Expected**: Project field shows \"Mobile App\".\n1352:- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open. Issues \"ENG-1: Setup project\", \"ENG-2: Design database\" exist.\n1354:- **Expected**: The selector filters to show \"ENG-1: Setup project\".\n1358:- **Action**: User clicks the Parent issue selector and selects \"ENG-1: Setup project\"\n1359:- **Expected**: Parent issue field shows \"ENG-1: Setup project\".\n1397:- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open. User has filled in: Title \"Implement OAuth\", Description \"Add OAuth support\", Status \"Todo\", Priority \"High\", Assignee \"Alice Smith\", Labels \"Feature\", Project \"API Redesign\", Cycle \"Sprint 10\", Due date \"Mar 25, 2026\".\n1404:- **Expected**: The issue is created with title \"Quick bug fix\", status \"Backlog\", priority \"No Priority\", and no assignee/labels/project/cycle/due date. The new issue identifier is briefly shown. The modal closes.\n1412:- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open. Issue \"ENG-1: Setup project\" exists.\n1413:- **Action**: User enters title \"Write unit tests\", selects \"ENG-1: Setup project\" as parent issue, and clicks \"Create Issue\"\n1414:- **Expected**: The issue is created. When navigating to \"ENG-1: Setup project\" detail page, \"Write unit tests\" appears in the sub-issues section.\n1499:- **Expected**: An issue list is displayed below the progress stats using the same layout as the Team Issues page. Each issue row shows: priority icon, issue identifier (e.g., \"ENG-42\"), title (clickable), status icon, labels as colored badges, assignee avatar, due date, and project name. Issues are grouped by status by default.\n1617:## Projects Page (`/projects`)\n1619:**Components**: ProjectCard, ProjectFilters, CreateProjectModal\n1621:### ProjectCard\n1623:#### Test: Project card displays project name as clickable link\n1624:- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing `/projects`. A project \"Auth Rewrite\" exists.\n1625:- **Expected**: The project card displays the project name \"Auth Rewrite\" as clickable text.\n1626:- **Action**: User clicks the project name \"Auth Rewrite\"\n1627:- **Expected**: User is navigated to `/project/<projectId>` for the \"Auth Rewrite\" project.\n1629:#### Test: Project card displays status badge with correct styling\n1630:- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing `/projects`. Projects exist with statuses: \"Planned\", \"In Progress\", \"Completed\", \"Cancelled\".\n1631:- **Expected**: Each project card shows a status badge with th