[2026-03-14T19:59:27.037Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GYLQgi5XWT3yPgFDUYVMLp","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→import type { Context } from '@netlify/functions';\n     2→import { getSql } from './db';\n     3→import crypto from 'crypto';\n     4→\n     5→function hashPassword(password: string, salt: string): string {\n     6→  return crypto.pbkdf2Sync(password, salt, 10000, 64, 'sha512').toString('hex');\n     7→}\n     8→\n     9→function generateToken(): string {\n    10→  return crypto.randomBytes(48).toString('hex');\n    11→}\n    12→\n    13→export default async function handler(req: Request, _context: Context) {\n    14→  if (req.method !== 'POST') {\n    15→    return new Response(JSON.stringify({ error: 'Method not allowed' }), {\n    16→      status: 405,\n    17→      headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },\n    18→    });\n    19→  }\n    20→\n    21→  try {\n    22→    const { email, password } = await req.json();\n    23→\n    24→    if (!email || !password) {\n    25→      return new Response(JSON.stringify({ error: 'Email and password are required' }), {\n    26→        status: 400,\n    27→        headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },\n    28→      });\n    29→    }\n    30→\n    31→    const sql = getSql();\n    32→    const users = await sql`SELECT id, name, email, password_hash, password_salt FROM members WHERE email = ${email}`;\n    33→    const user = users[0];\n    34→\n    35→    if (!user) {\n    36→      return new Response(JSON.stringify({ error: 'Invalid email or password' }), {\n    37→        status: 401,\n    38→        headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },\n    39→      });\n    40→    }\n    41→\n    42→    const hashedAttempt = hashPassword(password, user.password_salt);\n    43→    if (hashedAttempt !== user.password_hash) {\n    44→      return new Response(JSON.stringify({ error: 'Invalid email or password' }), {\n    45→        status: 401,\n    46→        headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },\n    47→      });\n    48→    }\n    49→\n    50→    const token = generateToken();\n    51→    const expiresAt = new Date(Date.now() + 30 * 24 * 60 * 60 * 1000).toISOString();\n    52→\n    53→    await sql`INSERT INTO sessions (token, member_id, expires_at) VALUES (${token}, ${user.id}, ${expiresAt})`;\n    54→\n    55→    return new Response(JSON.stringify({\n    56→      user: { id: user.id, name: user.name, email: user.email },\n    57→      token,\n    58→    }), {\n    59→      status: 200,\n    60→      headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },\n    61→    });\n    62→  } catch (err) {\n    63→    console.error('Login error:', err);\n    64→    return new Response(JSON.stringify({ error: 'Internal server error' }), {\n    65→      status: 500,\n    66→      headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },\n    67→    });\n    68→  }\n    69→}\n    70→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_0117Tuu1QNw947AjWT71VE25","session_id":"54b4dc3a-146d-4ec6-8623-05191aa19d81","uuid":"52674cb2-1673-490c-b811-3df21dd9b1d1"}
[2026-03-14T19:59:43.428Z] {"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"afa8c96b2ead9f350","tool_use_id":"toolu_0117Tuu1QNw947AjWT71VE25","status":"completed","output_file":"","summary":"Read schema and existing patterns","usage":{"total_tokens":60154,"tool_uses":36,"duration_ms":53832},"uuid":"965b1761-75eb-452d-8a7c-4794e7170384","session_id":"54b4dc3a-146d-4ec6-8623-05191aa19d81"}
[2026-03-14T19:59:43.431Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0117Tuu1QNw947AjWT71VE25","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now let me create a comprehensive summary document with all the information:\n\n## Summary Report\n\nI've thoroughly analyzed the LinearClone application. Here's what I found:\n\n### 1. DATABASE SCHEMA\nInferred from backend functions (no explicit schema.sql file found, using Neon PostgreSQL):\n\n**Core Tables:**\n- `members` - Users with id, name, email, password_hash, password_salt\n- `sessions` - Authentication tokens with token, member_id, expires_at\n- `teams` - id, name, identifier (prefix), description, team_members\n- `team_members` - Join table (team_id, member_id)\n- `issues` - id, title, description, status, priority, number, team_id, assignee_id, project_id, cycle_id, parent_id, due_date, created_at, updated_at\n- `cycles` - id, name, start_date, end_date, team_id\n- `labels` - id, name, color\n- `issue_labels` - Join table (issue_id, label_id)\n- `projects` - id, name, status, lead, target_date, team assignments\n- `activity` - issue_id, member_id, action, field, new_value, created_at\n- `notifications` - member_id, type, message, issue_id, created_at\n\n**Location:** Database accessed via Neon serverless (`/repo/apps/LinearClone/netlify/functions/db.ts`)\n\n### 2. REPRESENTATIVE SLICE: cyclesSlice.ts\n**Path:** `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/slices/cyclesSlice.ts`\n\n**Pattern:**\n- Uses Redux Toolkit with `createSlice` and `createAsyncThunk`\n- Three async operations: `fetchCycles`, `fetchCycleIssues`, `createCycle`\n- All async thunks get token from `state.auth.token` via `getState()`\n- Bearer token auth: `Authorization: Bearer ${token}`\n- API calls to `/api/cycles` and `/api/cycle-issues`\n- State includes loading, error, detail states, groupBy/sortBy filters, selectedIds for bulk actions\n- Extra reducers handle pending/fulfilled/rejected cases\n- Syncs cycle issues with issues when they're modified\n\n### 3. REPRESENTATIVE BACKEND: cycles.ts\n**Path:** `/repo/apps/LinearClone/netlify/functions/cycles.ts`\n\n**Pattern:**\n- Netlify function (serverless)\n- Validates Bearer token from Authorization header\n- Queries sessions table to verify token validity and get member_id\n- GET: Returns cycles with computed stats (issue_count, done_count, in_progress_count, isActive status)\n- POST: Creates new cycle, validates required fields, returns 201 with new cycle\n- Joins issues table to compute stats dynamically\n- Uses Neon SQL tagged template literals\n- Returns consistent JSON structure with snake_case from DB, transformed to camelCase in response\n\n### 4. CSS PATTERN: CycleList.css\n**Path:** `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/components/CycleList.css`\n\n**Pattern:**\n- Uses CSS custom properties: `var(--color-text-primary)`, `var(--color-bg-surface)`, `var(--color-accent)`, `var(--color-border)`\n- Dark mode default (colors defined in parent stylesheet)\n- BEM-like naming: `.cycle-list-row`, `.cycle-list-row-active`, `.cycle-list-row-selected`\n- Flexbox layouts with gap spacing\n- Subtle transitions: `transition: background-color 150ms ease`\n- Responsive with min-width: 0 for flex children overflow handling\n- Visual states: hover, active, selected\n- Accent color: `var(--color-accent)` which is rgba(94, 106, 210) - Linear's purple-blue\n- Compact spacing: 12px padding, 8px gaps\n\n### 5. APP ROUTING SETUP\n**Entry Point:** The frontend is deployed on Netlify. Routes are handled by React Router with pages:\n- `/login` - LoginForm page\n- `/signup` - SignUpForm page\n- `/my-issues` - MyIssues page\n- `/inbox` - Inbox page\n- `/team/:teamId/issues` - TeamIssues page\n- `/team/:teamId/cycles` - ActiveCycle page\n- `/issue/:issueId` - IssueDetail page\n\n**Store Setup:** `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/store.ts`\nRedux store with slices: auth, ui, teams, workspace, notifications, issues, labels, teamIssues, issueDetail, cycles\n\n### 6. AUTHSLICE TOKEN PATTERN\n**Path:** `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/slices/authSlice.ts`\n\n**Pattern:**\n- Token stored in localStorage: `localStorage.getItem('session_token')` and `localStorage.setItem('session_token', token)`\n- Initial state loads token from localStorage\n- login/signup async thunks call `/api/login` and `/api/signup` with email/password\n- Both return `{ user, token }` on success\n- Token is included in all subsequent API calls via `Authorization: Bearer ${token}`\n- Sessions expire server-side (30 days in login.ts)\n- fetchCurrentUser validates token and returns current user or clears auth on expiry\n- Logout action clears token and removes from localStorage\n\n### 7. TEAMSSLICE DATA MODEL\n**Path:** `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/slices/teamsSlice.ts`\n\n**Pattern:**\n- Team interface: `id`, `name`, `identifier`, `description`, `member_count`\n- Single async thunk: `fetchTeams` (no POST/PUT - teams are read-only in this context)\n- Stores array of teams in `items`\n- Standard loading/error/null pattern\n- No selectable state like cycles - just a list of available teams\n- Used to populate team navigation and selectors\n\n**Inferred from `/api/teams` response:** Returns `{ teams: Team[] }`\n\n### FILE LOCATIONS\n- Database connection: `/repo/apps/LinearClone/netlify/functions/db.ts`\n- Cycles backend: `/repo/apps/LinearClone/netlify/functions/cycles.ts`\n- Cycles frontend slice: `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/slices/cyclesSlice.ts`\n- Cycles component styles: `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/components/CycleList.css`\n- Auth slice: `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/slices/authSlice.ts`\n- Teams slice: `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/slices/teamsSlice.ts`\n- Store setup: `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/store.ts`\n- App spec/requirements: `/repo/apps/LinearClone/AppSpec.md`\n- Login backend: `/repo/apps/LinearClone/netlify/functions/login.ts`\n- Team issues backend: `/repo/apps/LinearClone/netlify/functions/team-issues.ts`\n- Cycle issues backend: `/repo/apps/LinearClone/netlify/functions/cycle-issues.ts`\n- Create issue backend: `/repo/apps/LinearClone/netlify/functions/create-issue.ts`\n- Pages (routing): `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/pages/` (ActiveCycle.tsx, TeamIssues.tsx, etc.)"},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: afa8c96b2ead9f350 (for resuming to continue this agent's work if needed)\n<usage>total_tokens: 61550\ntool_uses: 36\nduration_ms: 53837</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"54b4dc3a-146d-4ec6-8623-05191aa19d81","uuid":"58500718-0684-44de-a0b8-67d0ad55b6fd","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"In /repo/apps/LinearClone, I need to understand:\n1. The database schema - find and read the schema file (probably in scripts/schema.ts or similar)\n2. Read a representative existing slice like cyclesSlice.ts to understand the pattern\n3. Read a representative existing backend function like cycles.ts to understand the pattern\n4. Read any existing CSS files for components (e.g., CycleList.css) to understand the styling pattern\n5. Read the App.tsx routing setup\n6. Read the authSlice.ts to understand the token pattern\n7. Read the teamsSlice.ts to understand the teams data model\n\nBe thorough - read full contents of each file found.","agentId":"afa8c96b2ead9f350","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now let me create a comprehensive summary document with all the information:\n\n## Summary Report\n\nI've thoroughly analyzed the LinearClone application. Here's what I found:\n\n### 1. DATABASE SCHEMA\nInferred from backend functions (no explicit schema.sql file found, using Neon PostgreSQL):\n\n**Core Tables:**\n- `members` - Users with id, name, email, password_hash, password_salt\n- `sessions` - Authentication tokens with token, member_id, expires_at\n- `teams` - id, name, identifier (prefix), description, team_members\n- `team_members` - Join table (team_id, member_id)\n- `issues` - id, title, description, status, priority, number, team_id, assignee_id, project_id, cycle_id, parent_id, due_date, created_at, updated_at\n- `cycles` - id, name, start_date, end_date, team_id\n- `labels` - id, name, color\n- `issue_labels` - Join table (issue_id, label_id)\n- `projects` - id, name, status, lead, target_date, team assignments\n- `activity` - issue_id, member_id, action, field, new_value, created_at\n- `notifications` - member_id, type, message, issue_id, created_at\n\n**Location:** Database accessed via Neon serverless (`/repo/apps/LinearClone/netlify/functions/db.ts`)\n\n### 2. REPRESENTATIVE SLICE: cyclesSlice.ts\n**Path:** `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/slices/cyclesSlice.ts`\n\n**Pattern:**\n- Uses Redux Toolkit with `createSlice` and `createAsyncThunk`\n- Three async operations: `fetchCycles`, `fetchCycleIssues`, `createCycle`\n- All async thunks get token from `state.auth.token` via `getState()`\n- Bearer token auth: `Authorization: Bearer ${token}`\n- API calls to `/api/cycles` and `/api/cycle-issues`\n- State includes loading, error, detail states, groupBy/sortBy filters, selectedIds for bulk actions\n- Extra reducers handle pending/fulfilled/rejected cases\n- Syncs cycle issues with issues when they're modified\n\n### 3. REPRESENTATIVE BACKEND: cycles.ts\n**Path:** `/repo/apps/LinearClone/netlify/functions/cycles.ts`\n\n**Pattern:**\n- Netlify function (serverless)\n- Validates Bearer token from Authorization header\n- Queries sessions table to verify token validity and get member_id\n- GET: Returns cycles with computed stats (issue_count, done_count, in_progress_count, isActive status)\n- POST: Creates new cycle, validates required fields, returns 201 with new cycle\n- Joins issues table to compute stats dynamically\n- Uses Neon SQL tagged template literals\n- Returns consistent JSON structure with snake_case from DB, transformed to camelCase in response\n\n### 4. CSS PATTERN: CycleList.css\n**Path:** `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/components/CycleList.css`\n\n**Pattern:**\n- Uses CSS custom properties: `var(--color-text-primary)`, `var(--color-bg-surface)`, `var(--color-accent)`, `var(--color-border)`\n- Dark mode default (colors defined in parent stylesheet)\n- BEM-like naming: `.cycle-list-row`, `.cycle-list-row-active`, `.cycle-list-row-selected`\n- Flexbox layouts with gap spacing\n- Subtle transitions: `transition: background-color 150ms ease`\n- Responsive with min-width: 0 for flex children overflow handling\n- Visual states: hover, active, selected\n- Accent color: `var(--color-accent)` which is rgba(94, 106, 210) - Linear's purple-blue\n- Compact spacing: 12px padding, 8px gaps\n\n### 5. APP ROUTING SETUP\n**Entry Point:** The frontend is deployed on Netlify. Routes are handled by React Router with pages:\n- `/login` - LoginForm page\n- `/signup` - SignUpForm page\n- `/my-issues` - MyIssues page\n- `/inbox` - Inbox page\n- `/team/:teamId/issues` - TeamIssues page\n- `/team/:teamId/cycles` - ActiveCycle page\n- `/issue/:issueId` - IssueDetail page\n\n**Store Setup:** `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/store.ts`\nRedux store with slices: auth, ui, teams, workspace, notifications, issues, labels, teamIssues, issueDetail, cycles\n\n### 6. AUTHSLICE TOKEN PATTERN\n**Path:** `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/slices/authSlice.ts`\n\n**Pattern:**\n- Token stored in localStorage: `localStorage.getItem('session_token')` and `localStorage.setItem('session_token', token)`\n- Initial state loads token from localStorage\n- login/signup async thunks call `/api/login` and `/api/signup` with email/password\n- Both return `{ user, token }` on success\n- Token is included in all subsequent API calls via `Authorization: Bearer ${token}`\n- Sessions expire server-side (30 days in login.ts)\n- fetchCurrentUser validates token and returns current user or clears auth on expiry\n- Logout action clears token and removes from localStorage\n\n### 7. TEAMSSLICE DATA MODEL\n**Path:** `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/slices/teamsSlice.ts`\n\n**Pattern:**\n- Team interface: `id`, `name`, `identifier`, `description`, `member_count`\n- Single async thunk: `fetchTeams` (no POST/PUT - teams are read-only in this context)\n- Stores array of teams in `items`\n- Standard loading/error/null pattern\n- No selectable state like cycles - just a list of available teams\n- Used to populate team navigation and selectors\n\n**Inferred from `/api/teams` response:** Returns `{ teams: Team[] }`\n\n### FILE LOCATIONS\n- Database connection: `/repo/apps/LinearClone/netlify/functions/db.ts`\n- Cycles backend: `/repo/apps/LinearClone/netlify/functions/cycles.ts`\n- Cycles frontend slice: `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/slices/cyclesSlice.ts`\n- Cycles component styles: `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/components/CycleList.css`\n- Auth slice: `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/slices/authSlice.ts`\n- Teams slice: `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/slices/teamsSlice.ts`\n- Store setup: `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/store.ts`\n- App spec/requirements: `/repo/apps/LinearClone/AppSpec.md`\n- Login backend: `/repo/apps/LinearClone/netlify/functions/login.ts`\n- Team issues backend: `/repo/apps/LinearClone/netlify/functions/team-issues.ts`\n- Cycle issues backend: `/repo/apps/LinearClone/netlify/functions/cycle-issues.ts`\n- Create issue backend: `/repo/apps/LinearClone/netlify/functions/create-issue.ts`\n- Pages (routing): `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/pages/` (ActiveCycle.tsx, TeamIssues.tsx, etc.)"}],"totalDurationMs":53837,"totalTokens":61550,"totalToolUseCount":36,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10503,"cache_read_input_tokens":49262,"output_tokens":1784,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":10503},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"}}}
